
  [1mB. Inline in [38;5;153mapp.js[0m

  Add the key, the getter, and the minting directly to [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. No new file.

  - [1mBuys:[0m the smallest possible diff, and it satisfies today's literal request.
  - [1mCosts:[0m you told me other forms will need this. The second consumer either duplicates the logic or forces the
    extraction anyway — so you pay for A later, except with call sites already scattered. No boundary means no way to
    test identity separately from form handling.
  - [1mComplexity:[0m trivial.

  [1mC. A versioned session record instead of a bare id[0m

  Persist an object — [38;5;153m{ v, userId, source: "client" | "server", createdAt, lastLoginAt }[39m — under one key, rather than a
  naked string. [38;5;153mlogin()[39m still takes [38;5;153muserId[39m, and also stamps [38;5;153mlastLoginAt[39m.

  - [1mBuys:[0m the [38;5;153msource[39m field makes your unresolved backend question explicit and migrable rather than implicit, and the
    timestamps are arguably what "track who logged in" actually wants — an opaque id alone tells you nothing about when.
  - [1mCosts:[0m a schema you have to version and migrate, and more surface for future forms to learn. Over-built if the
    backend never arrives.
  - [1mComplexity:[0m moderate.

  [1mMy recommendation: A, borrowing exactly one thing from C[0m — store a versioned envelope ([38;5;153mv[39m, [38;5;153muserId[39m, [38;5;153msource[39m, [38;5;153mcreatedAt[39m)
  rather than a bare string, and keep the accessor returning just the id.

  The reason for A over B is your own constraint: "other forms will need it later too" is the sentence that makes the
  boundary worth having now, when there are zero call sites to migrate instead of several. The reason for borrowing from
  C rather than taking it whole is that "not sure yet" about the backend makes an unversioned bare string the one
  genuinely expensive thing to undo — a raw [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m string with no version tag gives you no safe way to detect and
  migrate old values later, and that costs one extra field today. The rest of C — [38;5;153mlastLoginAt[39m, reconciliation logic — is
  speculative until you know whether a server id is coming, so I'd leave it out under YAGNI.

  Does this shortlist look right before I take the recommendation into a sectioned design?

